{#
  ★★ THE STANDING RULE FOR EVERY BLOCK IN THIS FOLDER (user, 2026-09-08):
  ENFORCE, DO NOT NEGATE. Say what IS true of the body - a prohibition still puts
  the forbidden thing in the model's context. 0791 carries the full note and the
  worked examples. Comments are exempt; the RENDERED prose below is audited.
#}
{#
  VRTE DD/ZaZ Database - WHAT A RESTRAINT LEFT BEHIND.              (2026-09-10)

  THE USER: "keep the same thing, a state prompt in the LLM context window, except
  change it for how they feel after release according to how far the effect was.
  And only keep it for a couple of prompt, with subsequent one explaining the
  pain/ache is diminishing."

  This replaces the old ddz_aftermath short-lived EVENT. A device coming off is the
  AddOn's to narrate; what that device did to the body is awareness, so it lives
  here as a block in her own prompt while the body recovers.

  vrtedd_aftermath(uuid) returns, for the next THREE prompts after a device comes
  off - the same clock and 5-second floor as the ungagged countdown:
      1st   the phase line: how far the strain had got decides the wording
      2nd   the same line, easing        (phase 5: the deficit that follows it)
      3rd   what little remains, fading
  and then "". Each strain tier (arms, hands, legs, jaw, skin...) runs its own
  countdown, so an armbinder and a gag coming off together read as two sentences.
  It also runs out by game time (VRTE_DDZaZ_Scales.ini [aftermath]) if she is not
  part of any conversation in the meantime - she recovered unseen.

  An onlooker gets the outward signs, not this: vrtedd_aftermath_visible in 0950.

  Numbered 0790: after the state blocks (0780-0786), before the recoveries
  (0791-0794) and the gag (0795, always last), all before SkyrimNet's 0800.

  ⚠ Guarded with isString, never `!= ""` - an empty Papyrus decorator result
  arrives as an empty JSON object `{}`, and `{} != ""` is TRUE.
#}
{% if exists("npc") and existsIn(npc, "UUID") %}
{# ★ 1.3.0 (2026-09-14): STATE FILE FIRST, decorator as the fallback. VRTE_DDZaZ.dll writes
   Data/SKSE/Plugins/VRTE_DDZaZ/prompt_state.json the instant a device goes on or off, a name
   arrives, a restraint is released; read_json re-reads on the file's mtime and the random second
   argument defeats SkyrimNet's 55 s callback cache (VRTouchEvents' recipe, VR-verified, report 45).
   Matched on the SkyrimNet entity UUID. No entry for her = the old decorator path, unchanged. #}
{% set _ds = read_json("VRTE_DDZaZ/prompt_state", random * 10000 + random * 100 + random) %}
{% set _de = 0 %}
{% if isObject(_ds) and existsIn(_ds, "npcs") %}{% for _e in _ds.npcs %}{% if _e.uuid == npc.UUID %}{% set _de = _e %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}
{% if isObject(_de) and existsIn(_de, "after") %}{% set _vd_aft = _de.after %}{% else %}{% set _vd_aft = vrtedd_aftermath(npc.UUID) %}{% endif %}
{% if isString(_vd_aft) and _vd_aft != "" %}
{% set _p = "he" %}{% set _pp = "his" %}
{% if decnpc(npc.UUID).isFemale %}{% set _p = "she" %}{% set _pp = "her" %}{% endif %}
**WHAT THE RESTRAINT LEFT BEHIND — {{ decnpc(npc.UUID).name }}.** It is off now, and {{ _pp }} body is still coming back from it:

{{ _vd_aft }}

This is how {{ _pp }} body feels at this moment. It shows in how {{ _p }} moves, sits and carries {{ _pp }} weight, and it reaches {{ _pp }} words where it would naturally come up. How {{ _p }} feels about it is yours to play.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
